    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who registers as our premier start. Facing Pfaadt, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages and a high-probability stolen base environment against a slower-to-the-plate pitcher. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (74.78) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61) serve as our offensive pillars; **Yordan Alvarez** continues to dominate with an elite .458 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** capitalizes on a strong #3-hole assignment. We are also heavily leaning into speed and on-base volume at the top of the order with **Lars Nootbaar** (62.07), who sees a double-digit platoon bump against Holmes.\n\nThe most difficult sit-start decision involved **Carson Benge** (36.49), who fell just shy of our 40-point floor threshold. While **Carson Benge** maintains a strong base projection, the combination of a daunting 3.05 xERA matchup against Harrison and a negative platoon split (L/L) effectively neutralized his upside. Our rotation remains cautious regarding **Dillon Dingler** (44.07); though he remains in the lineup, his sub-50 score reflects the volatility of his dynamic platoon split against Legumina. We are monitoring lineup confirmations closely, specifically for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**; both are currently projected for aggressive scores against Kirby, but their value remains tethered to maintaining those prime #1 and #2 lineup spots. Should the actual lineups deviate, we are prepared to pivot to prevent unnecessary cap erosion, particularly as we maintain high defensive standards for bench pieces like **Chase Meidroth** and the inactive **Christian Yelich** and **Colt Keith**.",
